# Butterflies of Minas Gerais, Brazil, by genus, with a common species of each.
anartia      Anartia jatrophae, the white peacock of open fields
battus       Battus polydamas, the gold rim swallowtail
caligo       Caligo illioneus, the owl butterfly that flies at dusk
dryas        Dryas iulia, the orange Julia of forest edges
heliconius   Heliconius erato phyllis, the passion-vine butterfly
junonia      Junonia evarete, the tropical buckeye
methona      Methona themisto, the glasswing of the manaca tree
morpho       Morpho helenor, the blue morph of the Atlantic Forest
phoebis      Phoebis sennae, the cloudless sulphur
siproeta     Siproeta stelenes, the malachite
